= The Death of Henry Stone

Henry Stone, the former president who most americans blame for the Great Depression, has been found dead, apparently of suicide. 

The nation is largely indifferent to the despised Stone's passing. Obviously some communists and other radicals are fairly pleased by the whole thing, but even the most devout Republicans find it difficult to have much sorrow at the death of the man who left the nation in this state.

With Stone's demise, it seems as if an era of history is closing. The worst years of crisis are over, and the chaos and uncertainty seem to be finally easing. America is entering a new era, but what kind of era remains to be seen...
